      "content": "that's a really solid way to phrase it, the \"hidden tax\" thing is a good angle. but i'm worried about what people will say back. they'll probably argue that if you get rid of those rules, you're basically inviting companies to cut corners on things like food safety or building standards just to save a buck. how do i respond to the idea that these regs actually save us money in the long run by preventing disasters or health crises?",
